# Madam Eva, seer of the Tser Pool Vistani (docs/voice/madam_eva.md). The Tarokka reading (docs/contracts/campaign.md):
# `tarokka draw` deals the playthrough's five cards once; each `tarokka read <slot>` shows a card and Eva speaks its
# verse (data/tarokka/outcomes.json). The path: greeting -> the price (coin, a true thing, kin's thanks, Persuasion,
# a threat) -> the reading -> one question -> later visits (`again`: hear it again, a reading for one of you alone).

~ start
if flag.eva_reading_done
-> again
endif
if flag.tser_pool_brawl_won
-> after_brawl
endif
if flag.eva_met
-> return_visit
endif
set eva_met
quest madam_evas_reading invited
Narrator: Incense, candle smoke and old canvas. Behind a low table sits a woman so old she seems made of the same leather as her chair, shuffling a deck of cards without looking at it.
if flag.death_house_completed
Madam Eva [sly]: There you are. The house at the end of the village let you go. It doesn't, as a rule. Sit.
else
Madam Eva [sly]: There you are. I turned up a card for you three nights ago, and it has been tapping its foot ever since. Sit.
endif
interject name:ratatoille: Fortune-telling. Technically a branch of divination, but a very low branch. I'd nonetheless very much like to know how she does it.
if not flag.madam_eva_rumor
Madam Eva: Nobody sent you? No. The road sent you. It sends everyone to my table in the end; most of them simply don't stop.
endif
if guest:ireena
-> ireena_seen
endif
-> before_price

~ return_visit
if quest.madam_evas_reading == refused
Madam Eva [sly]: You came back. They always come back. The cards waited; they are better at it than you.
else
Madam Eva: Sit. We were in the middle of something.
endif
-> before_price

~ ireena_seen
set eva_recognized_ireena
Narrator: The shuffling stops. Madam Eva looks past you at Ireena for a long moment, the way you might look at a house you lived in as a child.
Madam Eva [sad]: So. You have come round again, child. Further along the road than last time.
Ireena: I've never been here in my life.
Madam Eva: No. Not in this one. Sit by the brazier; you are cold all the way through, and it isn't the weather.
if flag.tamsin_locket_recognized and name:tamsin_tealeaf
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: She means the locket. The woman in the locket. Doesn't she?
Madam Eva [sly]: Keep that stolen face in your pocket, little thief. Some faces belong to the dead, and the dead want them back.
endif
-> before_price

# --- The price ---

~ before_price
if flag.vistani_robbed and not flag.vistani_repaid
-> robbed
endif
if flag.stanimir_deceived
Madam Eva: You lied to Stanimir about his strongbox. He believed you; he is a kind man. I am not, but I will let it pass. Once.
endif
-> price

~ price
Madam Eva: The cards are free. The one who turns them is not. Ten gold, or one true thing that one of you has told nobody. The cards take either. They prefer the second.
if flag.nicu_kin_told and not flag.eva_caught_lying
Madam Eva [sad]: No. Put your purse away. You brought our Nicu home to his people, as much of him as the road left. That is paid already, and more.
set eva_reading_paid = "kin"
attitude madam_eva friendly
-> reading
endif
if flag.nicu_kin_told and flag.eva_caught_lying
attitude madam_eva friendly
Madam Eva: You brought our Nicu home, and then you lied to me at my own table. The one cancels the other. Pay like a stranger.
endif
-> price_menu

~ price_menu
* Pay ten gold. -> paid_coin
* [if not (gold >= 10)] We can't spare ten gold. -> poor
* One of us will tell you something true. -> truth
* [if not flag.eva_haggle_failed] [Persuasion DC 15] Read for us because the valley needs it, not for coin. -> free_ok | free_fail
* [Intimidation DC 18] Turn the cards, old woman. Now. -> threat_ok | threat_fail
* We didn't come for fortunes. -> refuse

~ paid_coin
gold -10
set eva_reading_paid = "coin"
Madam Eva: Gold. Honest, at least. The cards will take it. Sit closer.
-> reading

~ poor
Madam Eva [sly]: Then you are like everyone else in this valley. A true thing, then. Barovia has not found a way to tax those yet.
-> truth

~ truth
Madam Eva: Who pays? Not something clever. Something that costs you to say out loud.
* [name:godrick_pendlebrook] Admit what he hides behind "my eyes are tired". -> truth_godrick
* [name:liriel_dawnsong] Admit what she's afraid of. -> truth_liriel
* [name:thistle] Admit the thing about towns. -> truth_thistle
* [name:ratatoille] Admit what he'd rather be. -> truth_ratatoille
* [name:wren_featherfoot] Admit what his master never finished. -> truth_wren
* [name:kip_smudgewick] Admit who signed the contract, and who didn't. -> truth_kip
* [name:ilse_varga] Report the fever. -> truth_ilse
* [name:hedda_ironvow] Admit what the mist did to her prayers. -> truth_hedda
* [name:silvain_aster] Admit why they really want the book. -> truth_silvain
* [name:tamsin_tealeaf] Admit the truth about the locket. -> truth_tamsin
* Lean close and tell her the thing you have never told the others. -> truth_other
* On second thought, no. -> price_menu

~ truth_godrick
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "godrick_pendlebrook"
Player: I can't read. Not proper. My name, and "ale", and "danger". Every letter we've had, I've said my eyes were tired and given it to someone else. My eyes are fine. I'm just slow.
Madam Eva: Slow. Ha. The cards have read for kings who could recite a library and could not read a face. You read faces, big one. That is the harder alphabet.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Oh, Godrick. We'll teach you. Every night, if you like. Be at peace.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +3: You stood by me when I told Madam Eva I can't read
inspire name:godrick_pendlebrook: paid Madam Eva in an honest truth
-> reading

~ truth_liriel
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "liriel_dawnsong"
Player: I'm frightened of the dark. I have been since I was small. A priestess of the dawn, and I sleep with a light on, and tell everyone it's devotion. And I've come to the darkest place in the world.
Madam Eva [sad]: Then you came on purpose to the thing you fear most, carrying a candle. Child, that is not a weakness. That is the whole of courage, in one sentence.
interject name:thistle: I'll sleep next to you, Sunbeam. Anything comes in the dark, I'll bite it.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You stood by me when I told Madam Eva I'm afraid of the dark
inspire name:liriel_dawnsong: paid Madam Eva in an honest truth
-> reading

~ truth_thistle
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "thistle"
Player: I like towns. Bit. Beds. The little cakes. People singing in the big room at the inn. And I don't fit in them, and I don't fit in the woods any more either. I don't fit anywhere.
Madam Eva [sly]: The Vistani have no house and no country and we fit everywhere the road goes. Belonging is not a place, wolf-girl. It is the people who save you a seat.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: You fit with us. You fit right next to me. Mostly because nobody else will arm-wrestle me.
approve thistle +3: You stood by me when I told Madam Eva I don't fit anywhere
inspire name:thistle: paid Madam Eva in an honest truth
-> reading

~ truth_ratatoille
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "ratatoille"
Player: I'd rather cook than cast. I always would. I learned magic so people would sit with me, and I'm good at it, and I'd still rather be in a kitchen. That's a terrible thing for a wizard to say.
Madam Eva: Is it? The best wizard I ever read for burned his own beard making me an omelette. He was happier holding that pan than any staff.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I'm telling everyone. No, I'm not. Yes I am. No, I'm not.
approve ratatoille +3: You stood by me when I told Madam Eva I'd rather cook
inspire name:ratatoille: paid Madam Eva in an honest truth
-> reading

~ truth_wren
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "wren_featherfoot"
Player: My master died before my last lesson. I asked him what it was and he said it was in a letter I'm not allowed to read. I make jokes all day so nobody notices I'm not finished.
Madam Eva [sad]: Everybody is not finished, little acrobat. The ones who think they are, they are the ones the cards worry about.
interject name:ratatoille: For what it's worth, I'd noticed. I didn't say anything. I'm not good at saying things. I'd have made you soup.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You stood by me when I told Madam Eva I'm not finished
inspire name:wren_featherfoot: paid Madam Eva in an honest truth
-> reading

~ truth_kip
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "kip_smudgewick"
Player: My dad sent the devil away from our gate. Told him we'd manage. I went after him down the lane and signed behind Dad's back. I came home and said the orchard came back on its own. He went to temple and gave thanks for it. I've been lying to him for two years.
Madam Eva: You sold yourself to save a man who would not let you. That is a terrible bargain and a very good son. The cards will take it. They like a good son.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Kip. Thank you for telling us. We'll get you home to tell him yourself.
approve kip_smudgewick +3: You stood by me when I told Madam Eva who signed the contract
inspire name:kip_smudgewick: paid Madam Eva in an honest truth
-> reading

~ truth_other
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "other"
Narrator: {name} leans across the table and says it low, so that only the old woman hears. It takes longer than you'd expect, and {name} does not look at anyone afterwards.
Madam Eva: Yes. That will do. Keep the rest of it; you will need something to carry.
-> reading

~ free_ok
set eva_reading_paid = "free"
Madam Eva [sly]: For the valley. Ha! Nobody has said that to me in sixty years. Very well. The valley can owe me. It already owes me a great deal.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: You asked Madam Eva to read for the valley's sake
-> reading

~ free_fail
set eva_haggle_failed
Madam Eva: The valley has needed things for four hundred years, and still the candles cost money. Pay, or tell me something true.
-> price_menu

~ threat_ok
set eva_threatened
set eva_reading_paid = "forced"
attitude madam_eva hostile
Narrator: For a heartbeat something old and very cold looks out of her eyes. Then she laughs, a dry sound like a deck being cut.
Madam Eva [sly]: Brave. Stupid, but brave. Fine. The cards will speak to you, and you will wish you had paid them.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -3 liriel_dawnsong -2 kip_smudgewick -1 wren_featherfoot -1: You threatened an old woman for her cards
-> reading

~ threat_fail
set eva_threatened
Narrator: The tent flap opens behind you. Stanimir fills it, and he is not holding his fiddle. Outside, the music has stopped.
Madam Eva: You came into my tent and showed me your teeth. Now my family is showing you theirs. Choose again.
* Put the weapons away. We'll pay. -> threat_backdown
* Then we'll go through them. -> threat_fight

~ threat_backdown
Narrator: Stanimir steps back out without a word. After a while the fiddle starts again, a little slower than before.
Madam Eva: Better. The price has doubled. Twenty gold, or the true thing. The true thing has not doubled; the truth is never on sale.
* Pay twenty gold. -> paid_double
* One of us will tell you something true. -> truth

~ paid_double
gold -20
set eva_reading_paid = "coin"
Madam Eva: There. Expensive manners are still manners. Sit.
-> reading

~ threat_fight
set vistani_turned_hostile
attitude madam_eva hostile
attitude stanimir hostile
Madam Eva: Then go and do it. I will be here when you are finished. I always am.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -3 liriel_dawnsong -3 kip_smudgewick -3 wren_featherfoot -2: You turned on the Vistani in their own camp
-> END

~ refuse
quest madam_evas_reading refused
Madam Eva: As you like. The cards are patient. They have outlived everyone who walked away from them.
-> END

~ robbed
Madam Eva: Before we begin. One of you has forty of my nephew's gold pieces about you. The cards will not speak over the clink of them.
* Give it back. -> repay
* [Deception DC 18] We don't know what you mean. -> robbed_lie_ok | robbed_lie_fail
* It's ours now. -> robbed_keep

~ repay
gold -40
set vistani_repaid
Madam Eva: Good. The cards prefer clean hands. Cleaner hands. They are not fussy.
approve kip_smudgewick +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You gave the Vistani back what was taken from them
-> price

~ robbed_lie_ok
set stanimir_deceived
Madam Eva [sly]: Hm. Then perhaps the cards are mistaken. They are not. But perhaps.
-> price

~ robbed_lie_fail
set eva_caught_lying
Madam Eva: Liar. A bad one, which is almost to your credit. Give it back, or keep it and listen to what it costs you.
Narrator: She doesn't write it down. She doesn't need to; you watch her remember it.
* Give it back. -> repay
* Keep it. -> robbed_keep

~ robbed_keep
set eva_reading_paid = "forced"
attitude madam_eva hostile
Madam Eva: Then it is yours, and so is what comes with it. Remember that I said so. Sit. The cards will speak to thieves; they have spoken to worse.
approve kip_smudgewick -3 godrick_pendlebrook -2 wren_featherfoot -1 liriel_dawnsong -1: You kept what was stolen from the Vistani to their faces
-> reading

~ after_brawl
if not flag.eva_met
set eva_met
quest madam_evas_reading invited
endif
set eva_reading_paid = "forced"
Narrator: The camp outside is empty and the fire has burned low. Madam Eva has not moved from her table.
Madam Eva [sad]: You have bloodied my family and driven the rest into the trees. And still you come to my table. Sit. The cards do not care who deserves them.
-> reading

# --- The reading ---

~ reading
tarokka draw
cutscene madam_eva_reading
Narrator: She shuffles once, twice, and the cards whisper together like dry leaves. Then she deals five face down in the shape of a cross, and lays her hand flat beside them.
Madam Eva: Five cards. Three for what was lost, one for who will help you, one for where he waits. Don't touch them. Don't breathe on them. Listen.
if flag.eva_reading_paid == "forced"
Madam Eva: You did not pay what the cards asked. They will tell you anyway. They are not kind, and neither am I.
endif
Madam Eva: The first card is the past: a book in his own hand, the story of how he became what he is. Knowing it is a weapon. This one cuts him.
tarokka read tome
if name:ratatoille
interject name:ratatoille: His own hand. A primary source. A devil's diary. I would give my good skillet to read it.
elif class:wizard
interject class:wizard: A primary source. The devil kept a diary. Of course he did.
endif
Madam Eva: The second card is a holy thing, made by people who believed the sun would come back. In the right hands it makes the dead remember they are dead.
tarokka read symbol
if name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Made by people who believed the sun would come back. Then I'm not the first. Oh, I'm so glad I'm not the first.
elif class:cleric
interject class:cleric: A holy thing, still holding its light in this place. Then somebody kept faith here, once.
endif
Madam Eva: The third card is a blade. Not steel: daylight with an edge, once carried by the one he hated most. He cannot bear to look at it.
tarokka read sword
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: A sword made of daylight. Now that's a proper knight's sword. Right. Good. I understand swords.
elif class:fighter
interject class:fighter: A blade he can't stand to look at. I can work with that.
endif
Madam Eva: The fourth card is a friend. One who will stand beside you when the others run.
tarokka read ally
-> ally_seen

~ ally_seen
if tarokka.ally == darklord
Narrator: She looks at the card for a long time, and does not touch it again.
interject tag:blunt: Then we stand with each other.
interject class:cleric: We were never going to be alone. We have each other.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: No ally? That's all right. We've got us. Us is loads.
elif tarokka.ally.npc == ismark
if guest:ismark
Ismark: Me? The cards want me? Somebody tell the tavern. No, don't. They'll only laugh, and then they'll stop, and that will be worse.
else
interject tag:loyal: Ismark. The one they call the Lesser. Then we go back for him, or he comes to us.
endif
if guest:ireena
Ireena [smile]: I could have told you that for free.
endif
elif tarokka.ally.npc == kolyan_indirovich
if guest:ireena
Ireena [afraid]: My father is in the ground. We put him there. I watched the earth go on.
Madam Eva [sad]: Earth is a door, child. Most doors open both ways, if someone pays the toll.
else
interject class:cleric: A dead man for an ally. Calling a soul back is no small mercy, and no cheap one.
endif
elif tarokka.ally.npc == parriwimple
interject name:thistle: The big soft one from the shop? He gave me a biscuit. He's good. He smells like flour and sad.
elif tarokka.ally.region == vallaki
if guest:ireena
Ireena: Vallaki. Where we were going anyway. At least the cards are economical.
endif
elif tarokka.ally.npc == ezmerelda
Madam Eva: That one is my people's own. She left the wagons to hunt the things that hunt us. If you find her, tell her the old woman says to eat something.
elif tarokka.ally.npc == arabelle
Madam Eva [sad]: A child of ours. Don't sit here listening to me. When we're done, go.
endif
Madam Eva: The last card. Where the darkness will be waiting when you come for him. And you will come for him; the cards are very sure of that part.
tarokka read enemy
Narrator: The candles lean, all together, as if someone has opened a door. Nobody has.
Madam Eva [sad]: There. That is the shape of it. Three things lost, a friend, and the room at the end. Everything else, you will have to do yourselves.
set eva_reading_done
quest find_the_tome foretold
quest find_the_holy_symbol foretold
quest find_the_sunsword foretold
quest find_the_ally foretold
quest strahds_lair foretold
quest madam_evas_reading read
if flag.eva_reading_paid != "forced"
attitude madam_eva friendly
endif
-> treasure_here

~ treasure_here
if tarokka.tome == stars_2 or tarokka.symbol == stars_2 or tarokka.sword == stars_2
Madam Eva [sly]: And one of the three, you need not walk a step for. The cards put it in my keeping long ago, and told me to wait for the right hands. My hands are tired.
Narrator: She unlocks the iron-bound chest behind her with a key she keeps on a cord round her neck, lifts out a bundle of oilcloth, and sets it on the table between the cards.
if tarokka.tome == stars_2
Narrator: Inside lies a heavy book bound in black leather, clasped in tarnished silver. Nobody wants to be the first to touch it.
interject name:ratatoille: I'll... I'll touch it. Carefully. Like a soufflé.
give tome_of_strahd
quest find_the_tome found
elif tarokka.symbol == stars_2
Narrator: Inside lies a platinum sunburst with a raven at its heart. Even through the oilcloth, it is warm.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Oh. It's warm. Even here, it's warm.
give holy_symbol_of_ravenkind
quest find_the_holy_symbol found
else
Narrator: Inside lies a sword hilt of pale platinum with a sunburst guard and no blade. The candles burn a little brighter while it is uncovered.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: No blade? I'll hold it anyway. Somebody ought to.
give sunsword
quest find_the_sunsword found
endif
set tser_treasure_given
endif
-> question

# --- One question more ---

~ question
Madam Eva: One question more, and then the cards sleep. Only one. Choose it well; I am old, and I don't repeat myself for free.
* [if guest:ireena] What does he want with Ireena? -> q_ireena
* How do we leave Barovia? -> q_escape
* How is he destroyed? -> q_weakness
* [name:godrick_pendlebrook] Is the Order of the Silver Dragon still in this land? -> q_order
* [name:liriel_dawnsong] Will dawn ever come to this valley? -> q_dawn
* [name:thistle] Is Grandda Fen alive? -> q_fen
* [name:ratatoille] Where is the Wizard of Wines? -> q_wizard
* [name:wren_featherfoot] Where is Kasimir? -> q_kasimir
* [name:kip_smudgewick] Is there a way out of my contract? -> q_contract
* [name:ilse_varga] Where is Kestrel Company? -> q_kestrel
* [name:tamsin_tealeaf] Who is the woman in the locket? -> q_locket
* [name:hedda_ironvow] Will dawn ever come to this valley? -> q_dawn
* [name:silvain_aster] Is Aurel Mirescu alive? -> q_aurel
* Why were we brought here? -> q_why
* We've heard enough. -> q_none

~ q_ireena
set eva_question = "ireena"
Madam Eva: He wants what he has always wanted: a woman who told him no, long ago, and keeps being born to tell him again. Keep her away from high places and still water. She has fallen before.
Ireena [afraid]: I dream about falling. Every time I close my eyes near a window.
Madam Eva [sad]: Then you know more than he would like. Good. Hold on to that.
-> farewell

~ q_escape
set eva_question = "escape"
Madam Eva: The mists open for my people and for the dead. When the devil is truly ended, they will open for you. There is no other door. People have looked. You walked past some of them in the village churchyard.
-> farewell

~ q_weakness
set eva_question = "weakness"
Madam Eva: The things the cards named, in the hands the cards named, in the room the cards named. He has been hurt before. He has never been hurt by all of it at once. And sunlight. Always sunlight.
interject tag:veteran: Three items, one ally, one room. That's a plan. I've followed worse.
-> farewell

~ q_order
set eva_question = "order"
Madam Eva [sly]: The dragon's knights keep their watch still, big one, on a hill where the house is burned and the dead lay the table every night. Their master will not knight you. One of them will. Look low on the wall.
Player: Low on the wall. Right. Is that a riddle? I'm bad at riddles.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +3: You spent Madam Eva's question on the Order for me
-> farewell

~ q_dawn
set eva_question = "dawn"
Madam Eva: Dawn comes to this valley every day, priestess. It simply never arrives. Somebody has to carry it the last of the way, into his house.
Player: Then I'll carry it. I've carried it this far.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You spent Madam Eva's question on the dawn for me
-> farewell

~ q_fen
set eva_question = "fen"
Madam Eva [sad]: Your old trapper is alive, wolf-girl. He walks on more legs than he left home with, some nights. He is waiting where the wolves wait, above the lake. He told you to run. Don't.
Player: Wasn't going to.
approve thistle +3: You spent Madam Eva's question on Grandda Fen
-> farewell

~ q_wizard
set eva_question = "wizard"
Madam Eva [sly]: The wizard you want pays his debts in green stones and plays games against nobody, up where the snow is. You will find his name in a cellar before you find him on a mountain. And you will not like either.
Player: A cellar. A mountain. Right. I'll take notes. I'm writing this down. Somebody hold my skillet.
approve ratatoille +3: You spent Madam Eva's question on the Wizard of Wines for me
-> farewell

~ q_kasimir
set eva_question = "kasimir"
Madam Eva: The man you carry a letter for mends nets he will never cast, at a fire that is not his, outside the walled town. He has waited four hundred years for word from over the mountains. Don't make him wait longer.
Player: Four hundred years. Master Sorrel always did take his time with the post.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You spent Madam Eva's question on Kasimir for me
-> farewell

~ q_contract
set eva_question = "contract"
Madam Eva: Read it, merchant. Every word. Devils write in a hurry and expect their clients to sign in tears. The way out of a cage is very often written on the cage.
Player: Right. Read it. I can do that. I'll read it tonight. I'll read it tomorrow. I'll definitely read it.
approve kip_smudgewick +3: You spent Madam Eva's question on my contract
-> farewell

~ q_why
set eva_question = "why"
Madam Eva: Because he was bored, and he called. Because the cards wanted players. Because each of you was already walking toward the mist before you ever saw it. Pick whichever answer lets you sleep.
-> farewell

~ q_none
set eva_question = "none"
Madam Eva [sly]: Wise. Most people ask. Most people wish they hadn't.
-> farewell

~ farewell
if flag.eva_reading_paid == "forced"
Madam Eva: Now get out of my tent.
-> END
endif
Madam Eva: Go. Stanimir will feed you if you let him. And when you meet the devil on the road, as you will, be polite. It confuses him.
-> END

# --- Later visits ---

~ again
if flag.tser_pool_brawl_won
Madam Eva [sad]: You again. The camp is empty because of you, and the cards still haven't changed their minds. What do you want?
else
Madam Eva [sly]: Back again. The cards haven't changed their minds. I might have.
endif
-> again_menu

~ again_menu
* Say the reading again. -> reread
* [if attitude.madam_eva == friendly and option:respec] Read for one of us alone: a different road. -> personal
* Tell us about yourself. -> herself
* Your people and the castle: what are you to him? -> vistani_and_castle
* Goodbye. -> END

~ reread
Madam Eva: Once more, then, and slowly.
tarokka read tome
tarokka read symbol
tarokka read sword
tarokka read ally
tarokka read enemy
Madam Eva: The cards don't change. Only the people carrying them.
-> again_menu

~ personal
Madam Eva: One of you is walking a road that doesn't fit their feet. I can read them another. It costs nothing you will miss; not today. Choose who sits.
respec
Madam Eva: There. You are who you are now. Try not to waste it.
-> again_menu

~ herself
Madam Eva: I am old. Older than the walled town on the lake, older than the inn in the village, older than some of his walls. I knew him when he was young and only ambitious. That much you get for free.
interject name:ratatoille: That would make you... no. That isn't possible. Is it? It isn't. Is it?
Madam Eva [sly]: Many things here are not possible. Sit in enough of them and you stop counting.
-> again_menu

~ vistani_and_castle
Madam Eva: My people come and go through the mists, and he lets us. Long ago one of us did him a kindness. He has a long memory for kindness, and a longer one for the other thing.
Madam Eva: So yes, some of us carry tales up the hill. Be careful what you say at our fires. Be more careful what you say at other people's.
if flag.vistani_spies_suspected
interject tag:curious: The women in the village tavern were counting us. Heads, blades, purses. I knew it.
endif
if flag.stanimir_misdirects
Madam Eva: Stanimir has told the castle you went east. He thinks I don't know. Let him think it.
endif
-> again_menu

# --- The first four (owner, 2026-10-06: kept so older saves still play their quests) ---

~ truth_ilse
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "ilse_varga"
Player: Report. Kestrel Company marched into the fog without me. I had a fever. It wasn't bad enough to keep me back. I was tired of the work. That's all.
Madam Eva: And you have been counting heads ever since, so that nobody is ever missing again. Yes. That will do. That is worth more than gold.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Thank you for telling us, Ilse.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: For what it's worth, I'd have stayed in bed too. I'd have stayed in bed for a week.
-> reading

~ truth_hedda
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "hedda_ironvow"
if not (quest.cold_prayers >= cold)
quest cold_prayers cold
endif
Player: Since we crossed the mist, I have not felt my god. The prayers still answer. They answer cold. I have told no one, because a healer who doubts is a healer nobody lets near the bed.
Madam Eva [sad]: The Morninglord's light is a long way from here, priestess. It still reaches you. Ask why it reaches, not why it's cold.
interject name:silvain_aster: Hedda. For the record, those cold prayers have kept me alive twice. I will take cold.
-> reading

~ truth_silvain
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "silvain_aster"
Player: I tell everyone I want the book for the scholarship. I want it because Aurel went after it, and I would like to know whether my friend is alive. There. Somebody write that down.
Madam Eva: A scholar who came for a friend, and was ashamed of it. The cards like you better already.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: I knew it. I knew you liked him.
-> reading

~ truth_tamsin
set eva_reading_paid = "truth"
set eva_truth_teller = "tamsin_tealeaf"
Player: The locket. I'm good, but I'm not that good. Nobody leaves a coach that easy to rob. I think somebody put it where my hand would find it, so I'd carry it here.
Madam Eva [sly]: Somebody did. And now you have said it aloud, you can stop pretending you are only a thief. Good.
interject name:ilse_varga: Noted.
-> reading

~ q_kestrel
set eva_question = "kestrel"
Madam Eva: Some of your forty went into his house as guests and never came out as anything. Some walk his roads still, in colours that are not their own. You will see one before the end, sergeant. Count carefully.
Player: ...Noted.
-> farewell

~ q_locket
set eva_question = "locket"
if not (quest.the_locket >= her_name)
quest the_locket her_name
endif
Madam Eva: Her name was Tatyana. She is dead, and she is not. Whoever put her in your hand wanted you to carry her face home, and you have.
if guest:ireena
Ireena: Who is Tatyana?
Madam Eva [sly]: Ask him, child. He will tell you at great length, and every word will be a lie except her name.
elif flag.tamsin_locket_recognized
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Home. You mean the burgomaster's house. You mean Ireena.
Madam Eva: I mean what the cards mean. Put it away, now.
endif
-> farewell

~ q_aurel
set eva_question = "aurel"
Madam Eva: Your friend with the ink to his elbows went up to the castle to read. He is reading still. Whether he is still alive is a question even the cards find rude.
Player: That is not an answer. It is very nearly an answer. Thank you.
-> farewell
